    "Inject Dramatic Respiratory Pauses using punctuation syntax. While amateur creators let sentences run together into a continuous wall of sound, the master architect uses deliberate periods, ellipses, and em-dashes to force natural breathing cycles. A synthetic voice that takes a subtle, audible breath before delivering a heavy philosophical revelation fools the human brain completely, creating an irresistible impression of living, breathing humanity.",
    "Execute Multi-Take Generation for high-stakes script sections. Never settle for the first audio generation of your opening hook. Generate three distinct takes of the opening three sentences, adjusting emotional style sliders between each take. Audition the three takes side-by-side, selecting the take that possesses the sharpest vocal attack, the most compelling cadence, and the deepest emotional resonance to lead your video.",
